{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/40","id":5434975844,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVrsYR88AAAABQ_MmZA","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/40","diff_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/40.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran/PC5/pull/40.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/issues/40","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/40/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/40/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/issues/40/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SpicyBadran/PC5/statuses/8e3f0b642a92c2d2e27ba6d2a066803a70165697","number":40,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat(readme): generated progress matrix, and a post-merge duty to keep it current","user":{"login":"SpicyBadran","id":204524209,"node_id":"U_kgDODDDKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204524209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What the README now shows\n\nA seventh figure, `docs/assets/pc5-progress-matrix.svg`, and a sixth generated block,\n`<!-- pc5:matrix -->`. Both come out of one call to `progress_metrics()`: the drawing and the\ntext fallback cannot disagree because neither of them is written by hand.\n\nTwo columns, eight regions, one colour rule:\n\n| region | what it counts |\n|---|---|\n| Milestones by state | 35 cells, one per milestone, `M1 … M21` in graph order |\n| Evidence ladder | one row per level L1–L6, its own milestones |\n| Requirements, deliverables, filed evidence | 116 acceptance items, 66 named deliverable paths, 35 evidence paths |\n| Workstreams | 14 rows × one cell per milestone |\n| Platform-contract claims | 38 `PSM_*` ids by classification |\n| Platform-model operations | 64 operations over 10 interfaces, with what each withholds |\n| Blocked | the 6 blocked milestones beside the dependency that blocks each |\n| Committed validation records | 11 cells, each stamped with the commit it ran at |\n\nThe numbers it publishes today: **25.7% (9/35)** milestones verified · **87.5% (56/64)**\nmodelled operations implemented (8 refused by design) · **15.8% (6/38)** contract claims\nbacked by public documentation · **90.9% (10/11)** committed validation records passing ·\n**31/66** deliverables that exist as named paths · **19/35** milestones carrying an evidence\npath · **2/6** levels with a verified milestone · and **0 record(s) filed** for a physical\nboot, with `M19` reading `BLOCKED — nothing executed`.\n\nNothing was retyped to produce any of that: the figure and the table are what reading\n`roadmap.json`, `docs/evidence/**`, `psm/registry.py` and the contract gives.\n\n## It cannot be inflated\n\n* A cell is green only where a file in the repository records the thing. Levels 3–6 have no\n  green cell because `M11`–`M16` are `not_started` and no artifact claims more; a run at\n  level 1 is not painted as level 3.\n* Percentages appear only over finite counted sets, always as `NN.N% (n/m)`. `docs/` and the\n  block keep `stray_statistics()`: a `N checks`-shaped number in prose outside a generated\n  region fails the gate, which is the rule that made this figure necessary.\n* Documentation progress, synthetic/mocked coverage, host and emulator validation,\n  firmware-backed validation, physical-hardware validation and genuine Sony execution are\n  separate regions — the figure never lets a dense bottom half imply a sparse top one.\n* `tests/test_progress_matrix.py` (39 tests) recomputes every fraction straight from\n  `roadmap.json`, the records and the tree — deliberately *not* via `progress_metrics()` —\n  asserts the committed SVG equals a fresh render byte for byte, asserts determinism, and\n  proves the guard by tampering: painting a blocked cell green, hand-editing a README row,\n  and deleting the asset each make `presentation.py check` exit 1. Promoting `M19` in a copy\n  of the roadmap changes the drawing without anyone editing the drawing.\n\n## The part that keeps it alive after a merge\n\n`AGENTS.md` is new and is the authoritative instruction file for agents in this repository.\nIts rule: **after every successful merge into `main`, the agent must reconcile the progress\ndashboard without waiting to be asked** — detect the merge by full SHA from the fetched\nremote, read what landed from the diff, recalculate the affected figures from the\nauthoritative sources, `make presentation`, verify `presentation-check` + `docs-check` +\n`make check`, commit the dashboard on the same review path as any other change, and report\nwhich figures moved and which did not. The trigger is a merge: not a pushed branch, not an\nopened PR, not `mergeable=CLEAN`, not passing tests. Merging **someone else's** PR is the\nexplicit case. If the impact cannot be established, the policy says preserve the existing\nfigures and report the update as **outstanding** — never quietly skip, never estimate a\nnumber to fill a cell. It also rails the temptation shut: never merge in order to exercise\nthis, never inflate a state, criterion, evidence class or record, no force-push, no push to\n`main`.\n\nEnforcement is the gate, not the prose: `make check` already runs `presentation-check`\n(`check: unit psm docs-check citations-check presentation-check brand-check`), so a stale\nfigure fails an ordinary test run, and `make presentation` stays the only target that writes.\n`make dashboard-reconcile` (new, read-only) prints the first-parent merges newer than the\ncommit at which the figure and the README blocks were last written and exits 1 while any is\nunprocessed — that is the \"did I forget\" check, since the repo has no active CI to run it for\nus. `make post-merge` runs the whole reconciliation. `CONTRIBUTING.md` points at `AGENTS.md`\ninstead of duplicating it, and no competing `CLAUDE.md` / `.cursorrules` / second policy file\nwas invented (a test asserts none appears).\n\n## Measured\n\n```\nmake check              Ran 968 tests … OK (skipped=109)        exit 0   (was 929)\nmake presentation-check PRESENTATION OK: 7 figures and 6 blocks current,\n                        13 status rows match roadmap.json, 11 validation record(s) read  exit 0\nmake docs-check         DOCS OK: 68 Markdown files, 36 make targets   exit 0\nmake citations-check    CITATIONS OK: 258 commit reference(s)         exit 0\nrendered SVG            1200x1163, 193 rects, 296 labels, min font 10 px,\n                        0 labels outside the canvas, 0 overlaps\n```\n\n`python3 tools/presentation.py sync` run twice: the second pass writes nothing.\n\n## Not established by this branch\n\n* No boot on physical hardware, and no genuine PlayStation 5 system software execution. The\n  two top rungs are empty and the figure says so; `M19` is drawn blocked, in red, with its\n  blockers named.\n* No active CI and no screenshot, so neither is claimed anywhere in these figures.\n* The 87.5% operation count measures what this repository's own platform model declares it\n  implements — a contract ratio, not compatibility with a console. The 15.8% claim figure\n  measures documentation confidence, not progress; `UNKNOWN` means unverified.\n* `docs/evidence/` holds only a template, so the physical-hardware region can only read 0.\n  That is the honest number, and it will stay 0 until a real machine's record is filed.\n\nDraft, left open for you to review and merge — nothing here was merged.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-22T02:43:43Z","updated_at":"2026-11-22T02:43:43Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"7537724c14fb2ad674e8c78ae29c9b17cc1a07d8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"SpicyBadran:feat/readme-progress-dashboard","ref":"feat/readme-progress-dashboard","repo":{"id":1455102023,"node_id":"R_kgDOVrsYRw","name":"PC5","full_name":"SpicyBadran/PC5","owner":{"login":"SpicyBadran","id":204524209,"node_id":"U_kgDODDDKsQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/204524209?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran","html_url":"https://github.com/SpicyBadran","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/SpicyBadran/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":null,"homepage":null,"language":"Python","visibility":"public","is_templat